AWS EC2 Hardware Failure Recovery

## Overview

A production monitoring system generated a **Critical** alert indicating that a Linux server had become unreachable due to **100% packet 
loss**. Initial investigation confirmed that the EC2 instance had stopped unexpectedly.

Further analysis identified that the interruption was caused by an **underlying AWS infrastructure hardware failure**. The issue was 
resolved by performing a **Stop/Start** operation, which migrated the instance to healthy physical hardware. After recovery, the server 
resumed normal operation without any application or service impact.

