# Root Cause

The incident was caused by an **underlying hardware failure within the AWS infrastructure**, resulting in the EC2 instance becoming 
unavailable.

Restarting the instance initiated an automatic migration to a healthy physical host, resolving the issue without requiring operating 
system or application changes.

---

# Outcome

* Successfully identified the issue as an AWS infrastructure hardware failure.
* Restored the production server through an EC2 Stop/Start operation.
* Verified automatic migration to healthy AWS hardware.
* Confirmed restoration of network connectivity and application availability.
* Cleared all monitoring alerts.
* Completed post-recovery validation with no recurring issues.

---

# Lessons Learned

* Continuous infrastructure monitoring enables rapid detection of server availability issues.
* AWS **System Status Checks** help distinguish infrastructure failures from operating system or application problems.
* Performing a **Stop/Start** operation on an affected EC2 instance can trigger migration to healthy hardware when the root cause is an 
  underlying infrastructure fault.
* Comprehensive post-recovery validation is essential to confirm that networking, monitoring, and application services have returned to 
  normal operation.

